 Member 3 (Obstetrician): Gynecologist (OB

Group 2 -  Diagnostic Evidence Team (DET)
 Member 1 (Clinical Microbiologist (Lead)): Oversees the collection and analysis of blood cultures and other specimens to identify the organism responsible for the infection, utilizing specific culture media and techniques.
 Member 2 (Hematologist): Assesses the patient's coagulopathy and thrombocytopenia while considering the implications of disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) related to infection and the findings of the acute phase reactants.
 Member 3 (Pathologist): Analyzes the results of any tissue samples (if obtained) and assists in determining the nature of the infection through histologic and molecular techniques.

Group 3 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
 Member 1 (Senior Consultant Infectious Disease Physician (Lead)): Provides final recommendations based on the combined input from IAT and DET, ensuring that the treatment plan aligns with best practices for managing severe infections.
 Member 2 (General Surgeon): Offers surgical consultation for potential interventions if an abscess or acute surgical condition is identified (such as an adnexal mass needing drainage).
 Member 3 (Pharmacist (Antimicrobial Stewardship)): Evaluates the proposed antibiotic regimens for appropriateness, considering local resistance patterns, and offers adjustments based on culture results and patient factors.


